Package: amber-desktop
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Hyperquader <hyperquader@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: ambrosia, copal, amberlin
Recommends: amber-odin, amber-ols, kat800
Suggests: amberlin-backend, amber-theme
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Hyperquader-Coders/amber-desktop
Description: Amber Linux suite, in one package
 Installs the three applications that make up Amber Linux on Linux Mint 22+:
 Ambrosia the store the others read, Copal the notes overlay, and Amberlin
 the launcher.
 .
 This package contains no files. It exists so the suite can be installed
 and kept together with one name, and so that removing it does not remove
 the applications — they stay until you remove them yourself.
 .
 kat800 is recommended rather than required. It is a terminal that happens to
 be one of Ambrosia's first D-Bus clients, not a part of this suite, and it
 belongs to its own project — so the suite installs it by default and works
 without it.
 .
 The shared pieces come in on their own: the applications depend on
 amber-fonts and amber-gtk4 directly, so those are not listed here. The
 Odin compiler and its language server are recommended rather than
 required, since running the suite does not need a toolchain. The speech
 backend is only suggested: it needs a model set that the archive does not
 carry.
 .
 The theme is suggested too, and deliberately no more than that. Amber Theme
 recolours the whole desktop rather than only these applications, so
 installing the suite should not repaint a system the owner did not ask to
 have repainted. It is there to be found by anyone who wants the look the
 applications were drawn against.
